A||N||3||Lou Christopher||V8 starter/water pump||||1||
Z||000000||Lou Christopher||06-17-2000||07:52 PM||||I am relatively new to this list but it has already been of great help.  According to the info I received I have an Archie conversion 350 in my 85 SE.  The starter would not properly engage the flex plate.  After a couple of days of laying under the car trying various shim combinations I find that the starter is not perpendicular to the flex plate.  Either the starter or the adapter must have a bad angle.  Anyone ever have this problem?  how about making a tapered shim to align the starter?  Any ideas how to measure that angle while laying under the car?  Any help would be apreciated.<BR>               Lou Christopher<BR> PS- After looking I did not like that pulley sticking out into the wheel well so I just ordered a mesier electric water pump.  I think it will also stick out into the wheel well but no belts to get dirty and the motor is sealed.  Any thoughts on this would also be appreciated.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||06-17-2000||08:44 PM||||My conversion uses a special Tilton starter and adaptor, I'm not sure of the details.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Spyder||06-18-2000||12:45 AM||||I also have the Tilton starter with a mounting bracket. If I remember right, I think I had to use a washer on one end of the bracket to angle it properly. <P>If you don’t want the electric pump in the wheel well, I have seen hoses ran to the inlet and outlets and the pump mounted near the old dog bone.||||reg||1
Z||000003||coyote||06-20-2000||08:32 AM||||If you really do have an archie kit, then the adapter will be nothing more than aan alumium block with 4 holes, that are offset from center, if this was installed incorrectly it would cause your problems. first thing i would do is mark the current orientation then remove the starter and adapter block. Check for square from side to side the ends do not matter.really there is nothing there that would cause the need for a shim unless the engin adapter plate or the bellhpusing was bent.<P>coyote<BR>||||reg||1
